#: ../../../guides/library_guide.rst:2
msgid "Using poethepoet as a library"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../guides/library_guide.rst:4
msgid ""
"Normally poethepoet would be installed as a tool or poetry plugin, but it "
"can also be used as a library to embed task runner capabilities into another "
"tool."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../guides/library_guide.rst:7
msgid ""
"The following script replicates the main functionality of the `poe` "
"standalone cli."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../guides/library_guide.rst:9
msgid ""
"import sys\n"
"\n"
"from poethepoet.app import PoeThePoet\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"if __name__ == \"__main__\":\n"
"    app = PoeThePoet()\n"
"    result = app(cli_args=sys.argv[1:])\n"
"    if result:\n"
"        sys.exit(result)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../guides/library_guide.rst:22
msgid ""
"The `PoeThePoet <https://github.com/nat-n/poethepoet/blob/main/poethepoet/"
"app.py>`_ class accepts various optional arguments to customize its behavior "
"as described below."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../guides/library_guide.rst:0
msgid "Parameters"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../../../../.conda/lib/python3.11/site-packages/poethepoet/app.py:docstring
#: of poethepoet.app.PoeThePoet:1
msgid ""
"The directory that poe should take as the current working directory, this "
"determines where to look for a pyproject.toml file, defaults to ``Path()."
"resolve()``"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../../../../.conda/lib/python3.11/site-packages/poethepoet/app.py:docstring
#: of poethepoet.app.PoeThePoet:7
msgid ""
"Either a dictionary with the same schema as a pyproject.toml file, or a "
"`PoeConfig <https://github.com/nat-n/poethepoet/blob/main/poethepoet/config/"
"config.py>`_ object to use as an alternative to loading config from a file."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../../../../.conda/lib/python3.11/site-packages/poethepoet/app.py:docstring
#: of poethepoet.app.PoeThePoet:13
msgid ""
"A stream for the application to write its own output to, defaults to sys."
"stdout"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../../../../.conda/lib/python3.11/site-packages/poethepoet/app.py:docstring
#: of poethepoet.app.PoeThePoet:17
msgid ""
"The path to the poetry virtualenv. If provided then it is used by the "
"`PoetryExecutor <https://github.com/nat-n/poethepoet/blob/main/poethepoet/"
"executor/poetry.py>`_, instead of having to execute poetry in a subprocess "
"to determine this."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../../../../.conda/lib/python3.11/site-packages/poethepoet/app.py:docstring
#: of poethepoet.app.PoeThePoet:23
msgid ""
"The name of the file to load tasks and configuration from. If not set then "
"poe will search for config by the following file names: pyproject.toml "
"poe_tasks.toml poe_tasks.yaml poe_tasks.json"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../../../../.conda/lib/python3.11/site-packages/poethepoet/app.py:docstring
#: of poethepoet.app.PoeThePoet:29
msgid ""
"The name of the program that is being run. This is used primarily when "
"outputting help messages, defaults to \"poe\""
msgstr ""

#: ../../../../../../.conda/lib/python3.11/site-packages/poethepoet/app.py:docstring
#: of poethepoet.app.PoeThePoet:34
msgid ""
"Optionally provide an alternative base environment for tasks to run with. If "
"no mapping is provided then ``os.environ`` is used."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../../../../.conda/lib/python3.11/site-packages/poethepoet/app.py:docstring
#: of poethepoet.app.PoeThePoet:39
msgid ""
"A sequence of identifiers for global arguments that should not be displayed "
"in the help message."
msgstr ""
